From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Polack <spolack+git@mailbox.org>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:01:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] esp32-pixelcast in the other slot: the board's OLED

The 128x32 SSD1306 at 0x3C on the I2C header (SDA 21, SCL 22) shows what
esp32-pixelcast's shows: the name, the network, Art-Net in and the frame
rate. The first configuration sets the I2C bus to those pins.

The render loop writes the four lines once a second and attaches the
panel to the bus, whose owner runs there too; a task of its own sends
the lines that changed, so the loop never waits on the bus. The bus
detaches it before it closes.
---
 esp32/main/pixelcast.cpp                  | 137 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/main.cpp                              |   4 +
 src/platform/esp32/platform_esp32_i2c.cpp |   8 ++
 3 files changed, 148 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

